// Writer-reversed.
//
// One thread writes 1 then 2 to x; a reader sees 2 and then 1.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence forbids, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     PC forbids. Coherence forbids it, and PC is stronger.
//     PRAM forbids. Slow forbids it, and PRAM is stronger.
//     Causal forbids. CC forbids it, and Causal is stronger.
//   the models' definitions:
//     CC forbids. x = 1 hb-precedes x = 2 at one location, x = 2 hb-precedes
//       the second load, and that load reads x = 1: weak-read-coherence.
//     Slow forbids. Once a value has been read, no earlier write to that
//       location by the same writer may be returned.
//     Local allows. Local constrains only a process's own operations; other
//       processes' writes may be seen in any order.
//     POCausal forbids. x = 1 is arbitrated before x = 2 by the writer's order,
//       and the second load has seen x = 2.
//     RYW allows. The reader wrote nothing.
//     MR allows. MR alone lets the second load's replica apply x = 2 before x =
//       1; ordering one session's writes is MW's, and MW does not constrain
//       visibility.
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//     WFR allows. The writer reads nothing and the reader writes nothing.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  x := 2
} ||| {
  r0 := x;
  r1 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 2 && r1 = 1) [Local, RYW, MR, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 2 && r1 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, Coherence, RC11,
                           RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, CC, PC, PRAM, Causal, Slow,
                           POCausal]
